# REUSED: the same audit run a second time against the store the first one wrote. It is the only recording of what the tool says about work it did NOT do — the walk re-resolved and found identical, the scan served from a stored run, and what that run's reachability verdicts rest on. The date and the run identifier below are recorded literally, so a change to WHICH stored run answers moves this file. Its control is audit_text_populated, which must keep reading `derived by this run`.
$ kanonarion audit --gomod $AUDIT_PROJECT/go.mod --from-modcache=$MODCACHE
exit 0
